    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the owner API response so it satisfies the spec (\"upper-cased first letters of firstName and lastName, dot-separated with a trailing dot, e.g. `J.S.`\").\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\" +\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` endpoint returns an `OwnerDto` via this mapper, so `$.initials` now resolves to e.g. `J.S.` for \"john\"/\"smith\". `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
